Line 4: A constant can't work things out from a list.
    keep has_two as primes contains 2
                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
A constant can be a list written out, like "keep weekdays as a list of "Mon" and "Tue"" (and its length). To work something out from a list, use "let" instead of "keep".

Line 5: A fixed list can't hold lists, because those could change.
    keep grid as a list of (a list of 1) and (a list of 2)
                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Make it with "let" instead of "keep".

Line 6: A fixed list can't hold lists, because those could change.
    keep no_rows as an empty list of lists of numbers
                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Make it with "let" instead of "keep".

Line 7: All the items of a list have to be the same kind: the first is a number, but this is text.
    keep mixed as a list of 1, "two" and 3
                               ^^^^^

